{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCurveDeriv","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoCurveDeriv","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ImplicitScalar","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Pow"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_hasDerivAt_root_nonvacuous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_hasDerivAt_root_nonvacuous","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCurveDeriv.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**Non-vacuity.** `exists_hasDerivAt_root` is an existence theorem, and one\nwhose hypotheses nothing satisfies proves nothing. They are satisfiable:\n`(x, y) = (0, 0)` lies on the curve, and `curveDy 0 0 = 1 ≠ 0`.\n\nThe check with real content is numerical and lives in Route 26: along the\ntransport arc `|curveDy|` is bounded away from zero except at the branch point\n`φ₀`, where it vanishes — so the IFT applies on `[0,π] ∖ {φ₀}` and nowhere\nfails except exactly where `exists_unit_circle_disc_zero` says it must. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_hasDerivAt_root","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_hasDerivAt_root","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCurveDeriv.lean#L82-L101","doc":"**Off the discriminant locus, a root of the GGM curve is locally a\ndifferentiable function of `x`.**\n\nThis is `exists_hasDerivAt_implicit` specialised to the curve. The hypothesis\n`curveDy x₀ y₀ ≠ 0` is \"`y₀` is a simple root\"; it is exactly what fails at the\nbranch point on the transport arc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasStrictFDerivAt_curve","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.hasStrictFDerivAt_curve","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCurveDeriv.lean#L64-L80","doc":"**The curve is strictly differentiable in `(x, y)`**, with the stated partials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curveDy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curveDy","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCurveDeriv.lean#L61-L62","doc":"`∂(curve)/∂y` at `(x, y)`. Nonvanishing is exactly \"`y` is a simple root\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curveDx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curveDx","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoCurveDeriv.lean#L58-L59","doc":"`∂(curve)/∂x` at `(x, y)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}